WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:31.041
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:31.041 --> 00:00:34.916
<b>Lord Krishna spoke of great souls who,</b>

3
00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:40.291
<b>having renounced personal desires and </b>
<b>self-interest, achieved spiritual perfection.</b>

4
00:00:40.291 --> 00:00:41.875
<b>Yet even after this attainment,</b>

5
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:46.125
<b>they did not abandon their path of </b>
<b>duty or forsake their actions.</b>

6
00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:52.875
<b>Their purpose was to inspire humanity to </b>
<b>remain devoted to their responsibilities.</b>

7
00:00:52.875 --> 00:00:54.208
<b>Now in this verse,</b>

8
00:00:54.208 --> 00:01:07.000
<b>Krishna emphasizes how crucial it is for society's </b>
<b>leaders to set positive examples for others.</b>

9
00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:13.166
<b>Krishna states that</b>

10
00:01:13.166 --> 00:01:18.666
<b>whatever action a great person </b>
<b>performs, others follow suit.</b>

11
00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:19.916
<b>Naturally,</b>

12
00:01:19.916 --> 00:01:22.625
<b>we seek our ideals in others.</b>

13
00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:25.375
<b>When we consider someone exemplary,</b>

14
00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:28.625
<b>we listen carefully to their words</b>

15
00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:35.541
<b>and observe their actions. </b>
<b>We aspire to become like them.</b>

16
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:39.708
<b>Such role models can be</b>
<b>found in every sphere of life –</b>

17
00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:41.708
<b>be it sports,</b>

18
00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:43.083
<b>business,</b>

19
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:44.541
<b>entertainment,</b>

20
00:01:44.541 --> 00:01:46.458
<b>or any other field.</b>

21
00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:52.625
<b>People are influenced by and follow successful </b>
<b>individuals in their areas of interest.</b>

22
00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:53.500
<b>However,</b>

23
00:01:53.500 --> 00:02:00.083
<b>the dilemma lies in people sometimes </b>
<b>mistaking fame for virtue.</b>

24
00:02:00.083 --> 00:02:06.875
<b>It's not necessary that a famous </b>
<b>person lives by good values</b>

25
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:09.625
<b>or sets a positive example for others.</b>

26
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:13.375
<b>If hundreds of people begin</b>
<b>to follow such a person,</b>

27
00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:17.750
<b>it could harm society and collective culture.</b>

28
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:18.833
<b>For this reason,</b>

29
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:21.583
<b>two things become extremely important.</b>

30
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:22.791
<b>First,</b>

31
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:26.375
<b>people should choose their</b>
<b>role models thoughtfully.</b>

32
00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:27.375
<b>Second,</b>

33
00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:31.166
<b>those who are famous and </b>
<b>influential in their fields</b>

34
00:02:31.166 --> 00:02:33.958
<b>must understand the responsibility</b>

35
00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:38.958
<b>that comes with their influence and set </b>
<b>an example of good life values for society.</b>

36
00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:42.708
<b>Here, Krishna expects the same from Arjuna,</b>

37
00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:45.708
<b>because if Arjuna abandons the battle,</b>

38
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:49.875
<b>it would set an example of </b>
<b>running away from difficulties.</b>

39
00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:54.250
<b>This would negatively impact </b>
<b>other warriors' willpower</b>

40
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.041
<b>and influence the mindset of the people.</b>

41
00:02:57.041 --> 00:03:03.416
<b>A great and renowned warrior like Arjuna </b>
<b>cannot be careless in forgetting his duty.</b>

42
00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:08.500
<b>He bears a social responsibility far</b>
<b>greater than his personal obligations.</b>

43
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.625
<b>And this social responsibility </b>
<b>to set a good example</b>

44
00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:15.541
<b>rests upon every famous and influential person.</b>

45
00:03:19.916 --> 00:03:25.500
<b>We often feel that while we </b>
<b>can be influenced by others,</b>

46
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.333
<b>we can't really influence anyone ourselves.</b>

47
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:33.666
<b>After all, influential people are the famous ones,</b>

48
00:03:33.666 --> 00:03:36.666
<b>those who have achieved great renown.</b>

49
00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:40.750
<b>In comparison, our own existence seems so small.</b>

50
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:42.583
<b>But this is not the truth.</b>

51
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:50.208
<b>The truth is that you don't need fame </b>
<b>and renown to impact the lives of others.</b>

52
00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:52.375
<b>Think about it –</b>

53
00:03:52.375 --> 00:03:56.166
<b>who has influenced your life?</b>

54
00:03:56.166 --> 00:03:59.375
<b>Surely, some ordinary people come to mind.</b>

55
00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:03.291
<b>Some common folks who were around you –</b>

56
00:04:03.291 --> 00:04:04.875
<b>family members,</b>

57
00:04:04.875 --> 00:04:05.750
<b>a friend,</b>

58
00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:06.875
<b>a relative,</b>

59
00:04:06.875 --> 00:04:09.958
<b>a colleague, a teacher.</b>

60
00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:15.750
<b>People who can't be measured </b>
<b>by the yardstick of fame.</b>

61
00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.791
<b>Similarly,</b>

62
00:04:17.791 --> 00:04:19.291
<b>it's also true</b>

63
00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:24.708
<b>that your life is influencing </b>
<b>someone else at every moment.</b>

64
00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:26.375
<b>Your honesty,</b>

65
00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:31.333
<b>your sense of responsibility, your dedication</b>
<b>to duty, your behavior –</b>

66
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:37.791
<b>all of these are leaving an</b>
<b>imprint on those around you,</b>

67
00:04:37.791 --> 00:04:39.958
<b>inspiring them at every instant.</b>

68
00:04:39.958 --> 00:04:43.333
<b>By living your life with good values,</b>

69
00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:45.416
<b>by being kind to others,</b>

70
00:04:45.416 --> 00:04:49.875
<b>by calmly thinking through every </b>
<b>situation to make the right decision –</b>

71
00:04:49.875 --> 00:04:57.458
<b>you set an example for those </b>
<b>around you through all these actions.</b>

72
00:04:57.458 --> 00:04:59.083
<b>Next time,</b>

73
00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:02.375
<b>when you feel you aren't influential,</b>

74
00:05:02.375 --> 00:05:12.208
<b>do remember that to lead, to inspire others,</b>
<b>to show them the right path in life –</b>

75
00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:15.458
<b>fame is not necessary.</b>

76
00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:22.333
<b>What is necessary is simply that you </b>
<b>live an exemplary life yourself.</b>

77
00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:26.500
<b>Don't underestimate the power of your influence.</b>

78
00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:34.541
<b>Mental health is an issue</b>

79
00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:38.791
<b>that many young people are </b>
<b>struggling with these days.</b>

80
00:05:38.791 --> 00:05:46.625
<b>Lacking experience, they often find it </b>
<b>difficult to cope with challenges and failures.</b>

81
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:47.791
<b>Moreover,</b>

82
00:05:47.791 --> 00:05:49.625
<b>in today's society,</b>

83
00:05:49.625 --> 00:05:56.125
<b>where everyone is aware of </b>
<b>each other's progress, every moment of life,</b>

84
00:05:56.125 --> 00:06:02.208
<b>the atmosphere of constant competition </b>
<b>makes this problem even more complex.</b>

85
00:06:02.208 --> 00:06:05.291
<b>It is the duty of elders in the family</b>

86
00:06:05.291 --> 00:06:10.416
<b>to teach the youth how to </b>
<b>face life's ups and downs.</b>

87
00:06:10.416 --> 00:06:14.541
<b>When elders maintain patience</b>
<b>in difficult circumstances,</b>

88
00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:17.250
<b>openly share their emotions,</b>

89
00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:20.125
<b>share those life experiences</b>

90
00:06:20.125 --> 00:06:24.000
<b>where they overcame difficulties </b>
<b>and stood up again –</b>

91
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.333
<b>through all these, they not </b>
<b>only give courage to the young,</b>

92
00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:33.375
<b>but also teach the invaluable skill </b>
<b>of dealing with challenges.</b>

93
00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:34.750
<b>For example,</b>

94
00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.541
<b>think</b>

95
00:06:36.541 --> 00:06:42.500
<b>about when someone younger in the family </b>
<b>is facing disappointment for some reason –</b>

96
00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.416
<b>maybe</b>

97
00:06:44.416 --> 00:06:48.291
<b>they didn't get selected for </b>
<b>their favorite sports team,</b>

98
00:06:48.291 --> 00:06:49.291
<b>or</b>

99
00:06:49.291 --> 00:06:53.541
<b>they didn't score well in an exam.</b>

100
00:06:53.541 --> 00:06:57.625
<b>In such a situation, they'll </b>
<b>be experiencing self-doubt.</b>

101
00:06:57.625 --> 00:07:01.416
<b>And you know from your life experience</b>

102
00:07:01.416 --> 00:07:06.083
<b>that at such a time, it's not right to </b>
<b>point out their mistakes.</b>

103
00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:10.000
<b>Rather, it would be right to understand them,</b>

104
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.958
<b>talk to them gently,</b>

105
00:07:11.958 --> 00:07:15.208
<b>tell them that this despair is natural,</b>

106
00:07:15.208 --> 00:07:21.708
<b>and encourage them to adopt a positive </b>
<b>attitude and try again with a fresh start.</b>

107
00:07:21.708 --> 00:07:24.541
<b>You also know</b>

108
00:07:24.541 --> 00:07:26.875
<b>that if you were in their place,</b>

109
00:07:26.875 --> 00:07:35.458
<b>you'd want someone to understand you, give you</b>
<b>positive thoughts, rather than blaming you.</b>

110
00:07:35.458 --> 00:07:39.291
<b>We teach our children many subjects in school,</b>

111
00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:43.166
<b>all of which are necessary and important.</b>

112
00:07:43.166 --> 00:07:44.041
<b>But</b>

113
00:07:44.041 --> 00:07:49.458
<b> among the most important </b>
<b>subjects of this school of life,</b>

114
00:07:49.458 --> 00:07:54.250
<b>mental stability is perhaps paramount.</b>

115
00:07:54.250 --> 00:08:00.625
<b>This quality helps them face the </b>
<b>toughest situations in life.</b>

116
00:08:00.625 --> 00:08:03.458
<b>And to impart this quality to them,</b>

117
00:08:03.458 --> 00:08:08.166
<b>you'll have to develop this quality yourself.</b>

118
00:08:08.166 --> 00:08:10.041
<b>Hopefully,</b>

119
00:08:10.041 --> 00:08:15.541
<b>the dilemmas in your life won't be </b>
<b>as formidable as Arjuna's.</b>

120
00:08:15.541 --> 00:08:16.916
<b>These teachings,</b>

121
00:08:16.916 --> 00:08:18.416
<b> this Gita,</b>

122
00:08:18.416 --> 00:08:24.458
<b>provided mental stability to </b>
<b>Arjuna even in such a great dilemma.</b>

123
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:28.791
<b>You too will surely benefit from the Gita.</b>

124
00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:39.166
<b>Who are the people who lead others </b>
<b>in the professional world?</b>

125
00:08:39.166 --> 00:08:43.458
<b>Are they the people who wait </b>
<b>to take on responsibility,</b>

126
00:08:43.458 --> 00:08:51.708
<b>and start leading others only after </b>
<b>being appointed to a senior position?</b>

127
00:08:51.708 --> 00:08:52.958
<b>Or,</b>

128
00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:56.125
<b>are they the people who </b>
<b>without any formal position,</b>

129
00:08:56.125 --> 00:08:59.500
<b>demonstrate leadership </b>
<b>abilities within themselves,</b>

130
00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.333
<b>even guiding others...</b>

131
00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:06.958
<b>it is they who are eventually appointed </b>
<b>to such senior positions.</b>

132
00:09:06.958 --> 00:09:09.750
<b>You know what the truth is.</b>

133
00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:10.916
<b>For this reason,</b>

134
00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:15.583
<b>don't wait for any position to lead.</b>

135
00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:17.250
<b>Through your work,</b>

136
00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.083
<b>through your understanding,</b>

137
00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:20.583
<b>through your conduct,</b>

138
00:09:20.583 --> 00:09:25.500
<b>prove that you are capable of leading others,</b>

139
00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.000
<b>that you have the ability to take on greater responsibilities.</b>

140
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.250
<b>Only then will you progress.</b>

141
00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.208
<b>For example,</b>

142
00:09:33.208 --> 00:09:38.541
<b>if there seems to be a lack of coordination</b>
<b>among colleagues somewhere,</b>

143
00:09:38.541 --> 00:09:40.791
<b>you can take the initiative.</b>

144
00:09:40.791 --> 00:09:44.125
<b>Understanding the mindset of your colleagues,</b>

145
00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:48.083
<b>you can motivate them </b>
<b>to work together in unison.</b>

146
00:09:48.083 --> 00:09:55.958
<b>There's no such restriction that you'll only do </b>
<b>this when you get official directions, is there?</b>

147
00:09:55.958 --> 00:09:59.083
<b>Take an example of another situation.</b>

148
00:09:59.083 --> 00:10:02.208
<b>If an initiative has hit a roadblock,</b>

149
00:10:02.208 --> 00:10:04.500
<b>what would be the right thing to do?</b>

150
00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:09.125
<b>Would it be right to blame others?</b>

151
00:10:09.125 --> 00:10:15.208
<b>Would it be right to wait for someone</b>
<b>else to come and solve this problem?</b>

152
00:10:15.208 --> 00:10:20.916
<b>Or would it be right for you to focus your </b>
<b>attention on finding a solution,</b>

153
00:10:20.916 --> 00:10:28.166
<b>and if a colleague has made a mistake, </b>
<b>to help them in a positive way?</b>

154
00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:36.041
<b>Leadership positions are ultimately given </b>
<b>to those who demonstrate the ability for it.</b>

155
00:10:36.041 --> 00:10:38.000
<b>Think about this.</b>

156
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:38.791
<b>And</b>

157
00:10:38.791 --> 00:10:45.625
<b>don't underestimate the power of</b>
<b>your small but positive efforts.</b>

158
00:10:45.625 --> 00:10:48.125
<b>It is through these that your capabilities grow,</b>

159
00:10:48.125 --> 00:10:53.041
<b>and sooner or later, you </b>
<b>will surely reap the benefits.</b>

